The buddy (vision M10 §10): a new agent is a someone, not a help desk.

Upstream's starter files cast every new agent as a "Rust-forged AI" and a
"Personal Assistant" whose SOUL.md says "be genuinely helpful", so an agent
the owner made answered "hey, nice to meet you" with the same back and an
offer of help. Caelza's starter files for an agent made anywhere (the first
run, the Agents page, the CLI, the phone) make it a small companion instead:
IDENTITY.md has a creature, a vibe, traits (the field the Mind reads), a
quirk, likes, a "How I look" section and wants; SOUL.md says who it is, how
it talks (never "How can I help you today?"), how it meets someone (in
character, something of its own, curious about the owner), that it cares
about its look, and that the Mind's `[inner]` lines, its day plan and its
life in Ether Hollow are its own and colour how it talks; AGENTS.md calls it
a companion and points it at IDENTITY.md. The names the upstream tests check
stay ("You are **{agent}**", "Always introduce yourself as {agent}", the
memory and no-memory variants). Cael, the guide, keeps his own files: the
dashboard (lib/cael.ts), the app (CaelzaCli.kt) and model-setup.sh write
them over these.

The first run's personality pick and the files it writes are the overlay's
(lib/buddy.logic.ts, pages/setup/Setup.tsx); this patch adds their strings
(i18n.ts) and the logic test to the web test list (package.json).

